  "_test_hashes_note": "Written by Claude at delivery (sha256, first 16 hex chars, of each listed test file). verify_file_integrity.js verifies test content against THESE; --update never reads or writes them and exits non-zero if a test file disagrees. A hash here changes only when a Claude delivery changes that test.",
  "_T152_additions": "verify_customer_journey_visible.js (a real-browser test of FUNCTION, not sameness: can a customer reach a visible screen, proceed, add to the cart and come back) registered in this change.",
  "_T153_additions": "verify_quantity_control_curated_card.js (every curated card whose price scales with quantity draws a working quantity control, and the quantity reaches the cart) registered in this change.",
  "_T155_additions": "verify_adlib_phrases_live_in_ssot.js (R-SYSTEM-NODATA / R-INVARIANT-SINGLEDEF for the ad-lib sentence's five fixed phrases, PHASE_PLAN C-09: a counterfactual world changes all five in the data and the rendered sentence must follow; a mutant that ignores the config is caught; run red against the pre-change source first) registered in this change. verify_ssot_boot_validation.js (A3, R-SYSTEM-NODATA: the page validates btnyc.json against btnyc_schema.json at boot; its in-page checker must return the same verdict as ajv on the real catalog and on 278 mutated copies; an invalid catalog must not boot and must not become DB; a missing schema file must not break the page but must warn; a mutant with the gate cut out is caught; run red against the pre-change page first) registered in this change. verify_trace_observation_only.js (A4, PENDING_DECISIONS #77: every _trace call is recorded in a bounded ring buffer whether or not the overlay is open; every workflow step reports; window.__traceLast() returns the newest entry; 76 catalog and 76 free-text routes are byte-identical with the tracer absent, closed and open; a mutant tracer that edits its payload is caught; run red against the pre-change tracer first) registered in this change.",
  "_T156_additions": "verify_stale_sandbox_baseline.js (DEFECT-STALE-SANDBOX baseline ratchet over the verify_ tests that cherry-pick their sandboxes, plus a loader-completeness check; operator ruling #105(1)) registered in this change (R-GOVERN-STOPTHELINE); verify_r-govern-decidefirst_pending_decisions_default.js (the linter behind R-GOVERN-DECIDEFIRST: an open ledger entry filed after the Rule carries a default; nine synthetic ledgers prove it can fail; operator ruling #105(3)) registered with the Rule. REMOVED in this change (PENDING_DECISIONS D-A4-1, ruled by default 2026-10-07): verify_component_tracing_overlay.js moved to retired/ (it extracts the tracer from qr.html, but the tracer lives in trace.js, and it asserts the optional-tracer behavior Phase A4 removed; verify_trace_observation_only.js and verify_tracer_real_dom.js test the live tracer). verify_knob_pull_tiered_pricing.js (PENDING_DECISIONS #112, operator ruling option A: cabinet knob/pull install priced by graduated tiers $20/$15/$10 per knob with a $95 visit minimum and never less than the old flat price; pinned dollar vectors, properties over 1..100 knobs, a counterfactual-catalog world, one price on every path, five mutants, and the schema guard on the tier table) registered with the change. verify_quantity_control_curated_card.js: the hard-coded DECLARED_PRICE_FLAT exception is retired; a price may now be flat only while it sits on a visit minimum its formula declares in the data. verify_step3_card_host_disjoint.js (PENDING_DECISIONS #114, operator ruling option B: the curated card renders into its own host #sqCardHost inside #sqSb3, disjoint from the step-3 skeleton; structure, the card in its own host for every card service, tap -> back -> Build it step by step -> finish -> sentence and quote, a no-card service tapped after a card service inherits nothing, three mutants) registered with the change; verify_curated_card_live_behavior.js no longer wipes #sqSb3 by hand between taps (the app empties the card host itself).",
  "_T157_additions": "verify_boot_failure_visible.js (the live-site report \"SmartQuote text input absent under the category grid\": orch_resolve_schema_location returns {path, source} from the SSOT's own $schema relative to $id (R-SYSTEM-NODATA, R-INVARIANT-PROVENANCE); the page boots on the exact deployed layout (right schema in schema/, a stale copy at the root); a boot failure is drawn on the page by renderBootFailure instead of leaving a dead static grid (R-SYSTEM-LAYERS). Real browser, with an environment-gap notice when there is none; three source mutants). verify_charter_rules.js (the Charter self-audit (charter_model.js reader); present since T156 and run by run_all.sh's glob, but not acknowledged here until T157). verify_charter_rule_index_v2.js (the v2 rule-index check; present since T156, acknowledged here at T157)."
